# Deterministic checkouts on every platform.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF in
# the working tree. That silently breaks anything compared byte-for-byte: the
# compiler's golden disassembly is stored with LF, so a CRLF checkout made
# `golden: arithmetic.dart` fail on windows-latest while passing on Linux and
# macOS — the bytes on disk differed from the bytes committed.
#
# Determinism is a property this project asserts about its own output, so the
# checkout has to be deterministic first.

# Normalise every text file to LF in the working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact artifacts: compared verbatim by tests, so never EOL-converted.
*.golden -text
*.mod    -text
*.bundle -text
*.key    -text

# Binary assets.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary

# Windows-only scripts need CRLF to be runnable, if any are ever added.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
